WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:48.420
[Music]

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.120
The National Research Council was formed under an executive order

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.960
in order to mobilize the scientific knowledge of the country.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.060
The Food and Nutrition Board, formerly called the Committee on Food and Nutrition,

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:07.580
was formed in 1940 for the purpose of improving the nutritional fitness of the people in the war crisis.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:23.080
This presentation is designed to clarify and simplify
some of the newer aspects of nutrition for

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:29.300
the practicing physician, with special emphasis on diagnosis and treatment of vitamin deficiency states.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.280
The Council is indebted to these eminent authorities for the time and effort they have devoted to this task.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:47.160
Dr. Norman Jolliffe will speak
first on the recognition of vitamin deficiency states.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.060
Dr. Tom D. Spies will follow with a discussion of therapy.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:59.340
Dr. W.H. Sebrell, and Dr. Robert Goodhart

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.780
will then participate in the discussion of the immediate sociological and economic

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.709
significance of better nutrition. Dr. Jolliffe.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.580
[Dr. Norman Jolliffe:] Twenty years ago, 10
years ago, perhaps only yesterday,

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:20.960
patients with nicotinic acid deficiency encephalopathy may have been classified as wet brain,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.560
central neuritis, or atypical coma.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:26.689
These patients almost always died.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:32.020
Today, such patients can nearly always be promptly and permanently cured.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:38.180
Many people associate the terms scurvy, pellagra, beriberi, rickets

00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:42.590
or ariboflavinosis with dietary deficiency.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:47.829
It is not so well-known, however, that any of these conditions may occur in the presence

00:02:47.829 --> 00:02:52.349
of a diet which even by modern standards is
completely adequate.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:03:00.340
Deficiency diseases may be classified into two groups, primary malnutrition...

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.700
and secondary, or conditioned malnutrition.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.860
[Dr. Jolliffe writes the names of both conditions on the chalkboard.]

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:15.950
By primary malnutrition, we refer to deficiency states due to inadequate intake alone.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.660
[?] deficiency diseases, which come in this category,

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:23.620
are said to have a higher incidence in the south than in most other sections.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:29.140
Primary malnutrition, however, is found in all sections of our country.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:37.560
By secondary or conditioned malnutrition, we mean deficiency states produced by factors other than an inadequate diet.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.380
We shall list and discuss these several
factors.

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:46.969
First, interference with food intake.

00:03:46.969 --> 00:03:57.929
[Lecturer writes on a chalkboard, listing the points he is making.]

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:05.820
Many diseases interfere with an adequate intake of food. Fever, infection, surgery,

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:13.360
special diet such as prescribed for obesity, gallbladder disease or for diabetes, or kidney disease.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:22.120
Improperly-fitted dentures in elderly patients often prompt a selection of soft, easily masticated foods.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.480
The second factor is increased requirements.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:36.960
[Lecturer writes on chalkboard.]

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.190
When requirements are abnormally increased,
well beyond the usual or normal limits,

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:46.410
then increased requirement may be considered a conditioning factor.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:54.520
Fever, hard physical exertion, hyperthyroidism,
pregnancy, and lactation increase requirements.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.180
The next factor is malabsorption.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:04.060
[Lecturer writes on chalkboard.]

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:12.340
That is, failure to absorb. This factor is
frequently involved in conditioned malnutrition.

00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:18.949
The diet may be perfectly adequate, but because of failure to absorb, deficiency disease may result.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:25.580
Failure to absorb may be due to achlorhydria, so frequent in elderly persons.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:33.600
Diarrhea may interfere by promoting too-rapid transit of ingested food through the intestinal tract.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:40.660
Selective absorption by substances such as mineral oil may withhold certain vitamins from absorption.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.320
Mal-utilization.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:53.760
[Lecturer writes on chalkboard.]

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:59.160
Mal-utilization is often involved as a conditioning factor in malnutrition.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:06.759
Liver failure,  secondary disturbances of liver function from whatever cause, may interfere with utilization.

00:06:06.759 --> 00:06:13.159
The inability of many diabetics to convert carotene into vitamin A is an example.

00:06:13.159 --> 00:06:19.900
Any interference with the conversion of thiamine,
riboflavin, or nicotinic acid into the various

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:25.530
enzyme systems will precipitate deficiency disease as readily as an inadequate intake of food.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:33.830
In this boy of 15 who is a diabetic, the lesions at the angles of the mouth indicate riboflavin

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:42.630
deficiency to be a complication. Conditioned
malnutrition may be induced by hastened destruction.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:54.630
[Lecturer writes on chalkboard.]

00:06:54.760 --> 00:07:01.060
Certain of the vitamins are relatively unstable in an alkaline medium, notably ascorbic acid and thiamine.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:07.360
Alkaline therapy may be instrumental
in restricting availability of these two vitamins.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:13.260
In addition, ascorbic acid may be used by
the body to detoxify certain drugs.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.000
Next, hastened excretion.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:25.220
[Lecturer writes on chalkboard.]

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:30.900
Hastened excretion may be an important factor
in the production of malnutrition in patients

00:07:30.909 --> 00:07:35.869
where large amounts of fluid are forced, as in the treatment of diabetic acidosis,

00:07:35.869 --> 00:07:39.680
or in the treatment of infections with sulfonamides.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:46.499
In uncontrolled diabetes or in diabetes insipidus,
hastened excretion serves to deprive the body

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.199
of certain needed nutrients.

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:56.139
It is obvious therefore that the terms scurvy,
pellagra, and beriberi do not indicate necessarily

00:07:56.139 --> 00:08:01.729
a dietary inadequacy, for these conditions
may be as readily and as frequently produced

00:08:01.729 --> 00:08:06.199
by conditioning factors as by inadequate intake
alone.

00:08:06.199 --> 00:08:13.629
It is a tissue deficiency, whatever its cause, that produces nutritional deficiency disease.

00:08:13.629 --> 00:08:18.539
It follows that if a person has malabsorption, the physician may not correct it by giving

00:08:18.539 --> 00:08:24.259
any form of oral vitamin therapy, or if a
patient has mal-utilization,

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:29.860
any form of the vitamins may not improve the fundamental metabolic defect.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:35.579
Effective treatment of subjects having heart
disease, tuberculosis, or syphilis requires

00:08:35.579 --> 00:08:41.469
more information than is contained in the diagnostic labels of cardiac, tuberculosis,

00:08:41.469 --> 00:08:43.099
or [?].

00:08:43.099 --> 00:08:49.190
Likewise for subjects having vitamin deficiency diseases, effective therapy requires more

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:56.029
information than is given in the terms niacin, ascorbic acid, or thiamine deficiency,

00:08:56.029 --> 00:09:01.130
or is contained in the older terms of pellagra, scurvy, or beriberi.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:06.890
Therefore, as pointed out by [?],
each diagnosis of a specific deficiency

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:12.860
requires recognition of its velocity, its severity, and its pathogenesis.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:45.060
[Lecturer erases and then writes anew on chalkboard.]

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:56.310
By velocity is meant, whether it is acute,
subacute, or chronic.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:02.900
Of course, the acute or subacute may be superimposed upon chronic.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:07.120
Velocity is important for acute lesions.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:12.280
Those severe respond much more promptly than chronic lesions, though mild.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:18.760
Likewise, exact diagnosis and therapy requires a statement as to severity,

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:28.840
whether mild, moderate, or severe.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.700
Generally, mild deficiencies require less vigorous therapy than severe,

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:40.340
though the duration of therapy is more dependent upon velocity.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:52.840
Finally, the pathogenesis must be noted. That is, whether it is a primary or a conditioned,

00:10:52.840 --> 00:11:00.220
or a conditioned deficiency. Therefore, according to our hypothesis, a complete diagnosis of

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:05.740
one of the specific deficiency diseases will include one item under each of the following heads.

00:11:06.829 --> 00:11:15.709
For example, a niacin deficiency may be acute, subacute or chronic;

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:21.520
it may be mild, moderate or severe; it may be either primary or conditioned.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:29.900
And likewise, for ascorbic acid deficiency.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.100
This deficiency may be acute, subacute, or chronic...

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:39.020
either mild, moderate or severe,
and either primary or conditioned.

00:11:39.029 --> 00:11:43.980
And same way for all the other specific deficiency diseases

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:53.200
such as thiamine, riboflavin, and so forth.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:58.620
We are dealing here with tissue deficiencies which manifest themselves in three ways:

00:11:59.389 --> 00:12:04.129
By interference with the biochemical mechanism, as functional disturbances,

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:11.540
and finally, in anatomic lesions. The resolving clinical picture may be highly confusing.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:18.660
[Lecturer erases words on chalkboard.]

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:23.840
As a first step in clarification, let us chart the various degrees of malnutrition

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:28.260
from the standpoint of relative severity.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:33.220
[Lecturer begins drawing a line on the chalkboard.]

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:37.940
Let this line represent a normal tissue concentration of the vitamins.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:47.720
[He writes above, then below, the line on the chalkboard.]

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:52.660
The normal tissue concentration of any of
the vitamins.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:56.150
Let this line represent a mild deficiency.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:13:05.690
[He draws a second line underneath the first and writes above and below it.]

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:10.370
A mild tissue deficiency of any of the vitamins.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.870
[He draws a third line.]

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:16.260
Let this line represent a severe tissue deficiency,

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:24.200
[He writes above and below the third line.]

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:28.440
a severe tissue deficiency of any of the vitamins.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:35.240
To illustrate, let us take a mild ascorbic acid deficiency.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:44.040
If that mild ascorbic acid deficiency occurs
over a short period of time such as this,

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:50.449
we will have developed, then, a mild acute scurvy.

00:13:50.449 --> 00:13:56.869
On the other hand, if the tissue concentration falls to this level,

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:03.260
but over a long period of time, months or years,

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:12.000
then we will have in this patient a mild chronic ascorbic acid deficiency or scurvy.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:19.060
Now, let us illustrate the severe deficiencies by niacin deficiency or pellagra.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:25.160
If the tissue concentration falls over a short period of time to this level,

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:32.199
we will have an acute severe pellagrin or acute niacin deficiency.

00:14:32.199 --> 00:14:40.579
On the other hand, if the tissue concentrations fall to this same level but over a long period of time,

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:46.960
then we will have a patient who shows a chronic but severe niacin deficiency;

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:52.050
in other words, a chronic pellagra.

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:55.250
Here is a patient who exhibits the signs and symptoms

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:59.290
of an acute severe niacin or nicotinic acid deficiency.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:06.200
The stupor, the sucking and grasping reflexes, are the only outward expressions of the ailment.

00:15:06.209 --> 00:15:12.639
Superficial examination of the tongue, the mouth, the skin reveals nothing of diagnostic importance.

00:15:13.339 --> 00:15:19.370
Yet the therapeutic response of this patient
to niacin is almost as rapid as a response

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:24.259
of a patient in diabetic ketosis to fluids,
salt, and insulin.

00:15:24.259 --> 00:15:28.599
When the depletion of niacin in the tissues has not been as severe,

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:35.920
there appear the ordinary signs of pellagra, the red tongue, stomatitis, and dermatitis.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:43.030
This is ordinarily called acute pellagra, but in reality represents subacute severe niacin deficiency.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:52.080
Various other combinations are possible. For example, a mild chronic deficiency may have

00:15:52.089 --> 00:16:04.410
superimposed upon it an acute deficiency.
The pellagrin here illustrates such a situation.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:09.920
When first seen, this patient had the satiny
smooth glossitis and the dermatitis of a chronic

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:17.180
niacin deficiency. Following abdominal surgery,
failure to eat and glucose infusions, the

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:21.069
stupor and the sucking and grasping reflexes develop.

00:16:21.069 --> 00:16:27.680
They are signs of a severe acute niacin deficiency.
Treatment of this case with niacin has to

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:33.550
be modified as a result of the development
of a severe acute symptom.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.550
With adequate dosage, and this means large dosage,

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:42.340
these severe acute symptoms will probably respond to therapy in two or three days.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:45.660
The mild chronic symptoms, on the contrary,

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:48.380
respond very slowly.

00:16:48.389 --> 00:16:54.699
The pigmentation of the hands and the flattened
papillae of the tongue take months to respond.

00:16:54.699 --> 00:17:02.550
The principle demonstrated in the case of niacin applies to practically every nutritional deficiency.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:07.570
As another example, look at this case of severe
acute scurvy.

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:13.880
Now in this first case, an acute severe deficiency,

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:19.140
the tissue changes are largely represented by hyperemia, hemorrhage, and edema.

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:26.220
Our experience with cases of this type makes it possible to predict with full assurance,

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:33.640
that with adequate dosage, five hundred to a thousand milligrams daily, the outstanding symptoms in such cases

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:40.000
will disappear in about 72 hours and the gums shrink to almost normal position in about that time.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:47.980
With almost equal confidence, it can be predicted that this case of mild chronic ascorbic acid

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:52.539
deficiency will show slow response to therapy.

00:17:52.539 --> 00:17:57.839
The tissue changes are a response to a chronic deficiency, even though mild.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:05.920
Hypertrophy, or atrophy of the tissue, has time to develop, and response to therapy is very slow.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:13.020
For those who are inclined to take the diagnosis
of deficiency states casually, it should be

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:20.710
pointed out that we are faced simultaneously with one other problem, the problem of multiple deficiencies.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:27.660
One must acquire a facility for identifying the more common lesions of malnutrition.

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:31.620
Let us see and name some of them.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:34.010
You examine first the eyes.

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:38.860
With malnutrition known or suspected, you look for changes in the conjunctiva.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:45.080
This eye shows a typical cirrhosis conjunctiva.

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:52.780
Note its position in the equators at either side of the cornea.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:57.940
It is usually more marked on the nasal side.

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:06.040
Not all spots appearing in the conjunctiva on either side of the cornea represent cirrhosis conjunctiva.

00:19:06.049 --> 00:19:10.849
Some are synechiae and some are scleral deposits of varying composition.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:15.440
This lesion being chronic requires months of vitamin A therapy.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:21.880
These two eyes before and after show the results of vitamin A therapy

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:25.100
after persistent treatment for months.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.260
Note that the spot may appear more prominent after treatment

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:31.740
due to thinning of the conjunctiva around this part.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:37.700
In addition, the blood vessels in the sclera may also appear more prominent

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:40.760
due to this same thinning of the conjunctiva.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:44.580
The next thing to look for in the eye is corneal vascularity.

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:50.700
One needs either the biomicroscope and slit lamp or the small hand slit lamp.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:55.510
This corneal vascularity may be due to riboflavin deficiency.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:20:01.800
But light or other chroma or even other diseases may produce corneal vascularity,

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:08.000
so one again is confronted with making a differential diagnosis.

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:14.000
If the patient gives symptoms of burning, itching, tired eyes, and they respond fairly

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:21.059
rapidly to riboflavin therapy, one may postulate
the diagnosis of riboflavin deficiency.

00:20:21.059 --> 00:20:28.639
In this eye, one may see corneal vascularity but without the symptoms of itching, burning, and eye fatigue.

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:34.500
Response to riboflavin is slow and in many if not most subjects,

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:38.760
little response may be obtained in a year of therapy.

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:44.120
This may mean either that the corneal vascularity was not due to riboflavin deficiency,

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:48.820
it represents a relatively irreversible lesion.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:53.900
We come now to the mouth. In this patient, the lesions at the corners of the mouth

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:58.289
are typical of the cheilosis of riboflavin deficiency.

00:20:58.289 --> 00:21:03.389
Not all fissures in the angles of the mouth are due to a lack of riboflavin.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:10.500
In elderly patients, one often sees little fissures and cracks in the corners of the mouth.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:16.100
The lips cave in. She opens her mouth and one discovers the reason.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:25.039
Her need is not primarily for riboflavin, but for some serviceable dentures that she will keep in her mouth and use.

00:21:25.039 --> 00:21:30.999
Now let us go to the tongue. Two deficiencies are manifest in this organ.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:40.600
The most common is niacin deficiency. The earliest signs are red, swollen, fungiform papillae.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:48.570
As the deficiency continues, the filiform
papillae also become red, giving the scarlet-red tongue.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:53.180
This tongue shows what to expect in severe acute deficiency of niacin.

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:57.440
This is the  scarlet-red stomatitis of pellagra.

00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:04.520
The other extreme as represented by this tongue is that of a mild chronic niacin deficiency.

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:08.200
See the atrophy?

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:13.110
The papillae may be mushroomed out but are not so intensively red.

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:18.700
They may show fusion, or atrophy, and if this has gone on over several years,

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:25.980
you see fissuring, giving a geographic or scrotal type of tongue.

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:30.460
These tongues may or may not be associated
with pernicious anemia.

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:37.240
In any case, they often respond to niacin over long periods of time.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:43.159
This is not to infer of course that all tongues
showing geographism or scrotal distribution

00:22:43.159 --> 00:22:46.909
of the fissures are due only to a niacin deficiency.

00:22:46.909 --> 00:22:51.289
Many, possibly most, do respond to niacin.

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:56.120
Others are congenital, and still others may be the result of lichen planus

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:59.620
or other independent mouth lesions.

00:22:59.630 --> 00:23:00.890
In riboflavin deficiency,

00:23:00.890 --> 00:23:06.790
the tongue, instead of being red or coated, may develop a purplish or magenta hue.

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:10.200
Some observers have stated that pyridoxine deficiency

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:13.700
will produce the same appearance in the tongue.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:15.580
Now, the gums.

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:20.720
Let us briefly refresh our
memories as to how healthy gums appear.

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:28.420
Note the pointed intradental papillae. Note the healthy pink color of the gingiva.

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:32.780
There is no rosaceum or marginal redness.

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:39.950
And now for contrast, we have here the acute lesions of scurvy. As previously stated,

00:23:39.950 --> 00:23:45.980
when we give adequate doses of ascorbic acid, the gums will seem almost to melt away

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:49.340
as they return to their normal position and contour.

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:56.179
The lesions of mild scurvy are less definite.
Also, what role infection and calculi

00:23:56.179 --> 00:24:00.260
have to do with the production of these signs is not clear.

00:24:00.260 --> 00:24:05.770
It is probable that ascorbic acid deficiency
is a conditioning factor for many changes

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:10.350
that occur in the gums, but by no means all.

00:24:10.350 --> 00:24:16.620
For example, in this case of Vincent's infection, the primary diagnosis based upon the presence

00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:21.549
of the scarlet red stomatitis, is niacin deficiency.

00:24:21.549 --> 00:24:26.309
If specific therapy, in this instance niacin therapy, is instituted,

00:24:26.309 --> 00:24:31.820
not only will the scarlet red stomatitis be blanched within 24 to 48 hours,

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:36.420
but the Vincent's infection heals without other general or local therapy.

00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:42.540
Certain deficiency signs in the skin should be familiar to every physician.

00:24:42.820 --> 00:24:48.760
The dermatitis of pellagra, for example, although more common where the disease is endemic,

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:52.900
may be seen in patients in any section of the United States.

00:24:52.909 --> 00:24:58.970
Typically, as in this patient, the lesions
appear on the exposed parts of the backs

00:24:58.970 --> 00:25:05.310
of the hands, wrists, and forearms. It may appear on the neck or about the ankles.

00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:07.300
It is usually symmetrical.

00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:15.700
The areas may progress to ulceration, desquamation, and cracking and bleeding.

00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:20.120
Sunlight enhances the discomfort and the burning sensation.

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:26.000
The skin lesions associated with scurvy are the petechial or parafollicular hemorrhages,

00:25:26.140 --> 00:25:31.660
often on the lower extremities or in areas where the skin is subjected to pressure.

00:25:31.669 --> 00:25:37.779
A number of observers have described various
skin lesions which disappear after the administration

00:25:37.779 --> 00:25:41.429
of the whole vitamin B complex.

00:25:41.429 --> 00:25:45.549
Some of these lesions are of the nature of a chronic or acute eczema.

00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:51.520
Signs of vitamin  A deficiency are often observable in the skin.

00:25:51.620 --> 00:25:57.520
Here we see the hyper-folliculitis of vitamin A deficiency.

00:25:57.780 --> 00:26:03.320
Now, we shall consider the neurologic manifestations of malnutrition.

00:26:03.320 --> 00:26:09.100
A diagnosis of mild polyneuropathy may be made when neurologic examination discloses

00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:11.760
discloses the following signs.

00:26:12.600 --> 00:26:14.200
Calf muscle tenderness:

00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:21.940
The healthy calf muscle, if squeezed from behind so as not to include the tibia in the grip,

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:26.320
can tolerate considerable pressure before pain is felt.

00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:35.840
Pain occurs in the presence of a mild vitamin B1 deficiency, as this patient's face indicates.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:42.680
Plantar hyperesthesia: we refer here not to the ordinary tickling sensation

00:26:42.860 --> 00:26:47.160
usually elicited by scratching the undersurface of the foot.

00:26:47.160 --> 00:26:55.260
Plantar hyperesthesia is a very definite hyperesthetic
pain produced by drawing an object firmly

00:26:55.270 --> 00:26:58.750
but not un-gently over the bottom of the foot.

00:26:58.750 --> 00:27:03.810
How uncomfortable this becomes can be judged by the patient's facial reaction.

00:27:03.810 --> 00:27:14.659
If there is a mild polyneuropathy, vibratory sensation tested with a c256 tuning fork, becomes diminished.

00:27:14.659 --> 00:27:22.359
These three signs: calf muscle tenderness, plantar hyperesthesia, and diminished vibratory sensation,

00:27:22.380 --> 00:27:28.060
do not establish a positive diagnosis of polyneuropathy due to a general or systemic

00:27:28.070 --> 00:27:35.370
nutritional deficiency, since circulatory disturbances
may cause these or similar findings.

00:27:35.370 --> 00:27:42.430
If in addition, the ankle jerks are absent,
a diagnosis of mild polyneuropathy should be made.

00:27:42.540 --> 00:27:45.900
Note that the ankle jerks are absent in this patient.

00:27:46.420 --> 00:27:52.559
A diagnosis of moderate polyneuropathy may be made when knees and ankle jerks

00:27:52.559 --> 00:27:57.809
can no longer be elicited, but positive signs are still limited to the lower extremities.

00:27:59.300 --> 00:28:02.560
We shall see how this applies in this patient.

00:28:02.720 --> 00:28:07.360
Impairment of position sense in the toes is now quite definite.

00:28:07.370 --> 00:28:13.019
The gait is now frequently affected and the burning sensation, often noticed earlier

00:28:13.019 --> 00:28:17.539
but now quite acute in the soles of the feet, plus diminished position sense,

00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:23.940
may compel these patients to walk carefully, as if barefoot on a floor strewn with tacks.

00:28:23.950 --> 00:28:26.850
Calf muscle atrophy is now very obvious.

00:28:27.020 --> 00:28:32.320
Toe drop and foot drop are also plainly evident.

00:28:32.320 --> 00:28:35.720
Wrist drop soon appears.

00:28:42.880 --> 00:28:47.220
Walking, virtually impossible, is of a steppage type.

00:28:47.600 --> 00:28:56.100
As in thiamine deficiency, objective signs of niacin deficiency are often preceded by mental symptoms.

00:28:56.110 --> 00:29:02.730
These symptoms involve all forms of sensation, increased psychomotor activity, definite trends

00:29:02.730 --> 00:29:09.769
toward depression and apprehension and wariness,
fatigability, headaches, and insomnia.

00:29:09.769 --> 00:29:15.130
In patients with classic pellagra, the mental
symptoms commonly seen are those found in

00:29:15.130 --> 00:29:22.990
any organic psychosis. They include memory
defects, disorientation, confusion, and confabulation.

00:29:23.520 --> 00:29:32.179
Periods of excitement, depression, mania,
delirium, and paranoia occur not infrequently.

00:29:32.179 --> 00:29:37.159
These mental disorders may appear before other
signs of pellagra are evident.

00:29:37.159 --> 00:29:39.659
If the psychosis has been of short duration,

00:29:39.660 --> 00:29:43.900
response to treatment with niacin is usually prompt.

00:29:43.909 --> 00:29:48.289
Referring once again to our chart, it may
be pointed out that from the standpoint

00:29:48.289 --> 00:29:55.209
of niacin deficiency, the pellagra syndrome of stomatitis, mental symptoms, diarrhea

00:29:55.340 --> 00:30:02.460
and dermatitis represents a chronic partial deficiency of nicotinic acid.

00:30:02.460 --> 00:30:09.169
When the availability of niacin is suddenly reduced, and the restriction is virtually

00:30:09.169 --> 00:30:14.600
at complete deficiency, structural changes
may not have time to develop.

00:30:14.600 --> 00:30:18.580
And a fairly characteristic neuropsychiatric syndrome occurs

00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:23.460
which has been called nicotinic acid deficiency encephalopathy.

00:30:23.680 --> 00:30:30.100
In endemic pellagra, the encephalopathic syndrome occurs only in the most advanced and severe cases.

00:30:30.820 --> 00:30:35.760
The syndrome may occur as the only clinical manifestation of a deficiency disease,

00:30:36.160 --> 00:30:42.300
or it may occur in association with polyneuropathy, scurvy or ariboflavinosis.

00:30:43.380 --> 00:30:49.540
We may thus have an acute severe niacin deficiency superimposed upon deficiencies

00:30:49.540 --> 00:30:54.000
of almost any degree of the other water-soluble vitamins.

00:30:54.780 --> 00:30:59.120
Nearly every one of the patients we have studied had a multiple deficiency.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:06.000
This must follow by necessity, when we consider the fact that neither primary dietary failure

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:11.570
nor conditioning factors are as a rule selective
of any one vitamin.

00:31:11.570 --> 00:31:15.890
With the possible exceptions of vitamins D, E, and K,

00:31:16.160 --> 00:31:20.360
there can seldom be a diagnosis of a single vitamin deficiency.

00:31:20.840 --> 00:31:28.080
Sydenstricker, Williams and Wilder, Smith,
McLester and other investigators have observed

00:31:28.090 --> 00:31:35.310
and described subgross multiple deficiency states, sometimes loosely grouped as a neurasthenic syndrome.

00:31:36.360 --> 00:31:43.580
Such deficiency states no longer need remain in a dim realm of a subclinical or subgross.

00:31:43.580 --> 00:31:49.010
With the diagnostic methods now at hand, it is often possible to eliminate guesswork

00:31:49.010 --> 00:31:53.950
and opinion and to place our diagnosis upon a firm objective basis.

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:57.520
And now back to our conference.

00:31:58.380 --> 00:32:05.360
[Speaker 1:] Thank you Dr. Jolliffe. And now we shall hear from Dr. Spies on therapy, Dr. Spies.

00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:11.000
[Dr. Tom D. Spies:] Dr. Jolliffe has broken
new ground for us today with his able exposition

00:32:11.010 --> 00:32:15.610
of the relationships between the various deficiency
states.

00:32:15.610 --> 00:32:20.610
It is not surprising that a parallel statement
as to therapy has recently appeared

00:32:20.620 --> 00:32:24.059
from my good friend, Dr. V. P. Sydenstricker.

00:32:24.059 --> 00:32:29.939
We have long applied these principles in our work at Hillman Hospital.

00:32:30.020 --> 00:32:33.260
The following dosages are for adults.

00:32:33.380 --> 00:32:39.220
Suggested dosages for children are determined by proportional body weight.

00:32:39.220 --> 00:32:46.630
In treating the clinical syndromes of beriberi, pellagra, riboflavin deficiency and scurvy,

00:32:46.630 --> 00:32:54.470
we use a basic formula containing 10 milligrams of thiamine, 50 milligrams of niacin,

00:32:55.020 --> 00:33:02.200
five milligrams of riboflavin, and 75 milligrams of ascorbic acid.

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:09.120
When we find the symptoms of one deficiency
disease predominant, we add to the basic formula

00:33:09.120 --> 00:33:13.600
more of the vitamins specific for the predominating
deficiency.

00:33:13.600 --> 00:33:19.240
In beriberi, 10 milligrams of thiamine are
added daily.

00:33:19.240 --> 00:33:26.220
In riboflavin deficiency, five milligrams of riboflavin twice daily.

00:33:26.220 --> 00:33:33.000
In scurvy, 100 milligrams of ascorbic acid, three times a day.

00:33:33.060 --> 00:33:40.260
And in mild pellagra, 50 milligrams of
niacin amide three times a day.

00:33:40.260 --> 00:33:46.880
If the pellagra is severe, the patient is
given 150 milligrams of niacin amide

00:33:46.880 --> 00:33:52.399
three times a day in addition to the basic formula.

00:33:52.399 --> 00:33:57.659
When the patient is moribund, it may be necessary to resort to parenteral injection

00:33:57.660 --> 00:34:02.260
in order to prolong and indeed even to save life.

00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:08.370
When large amounts of D-glucose are injected
daily, we recommend inclusion of 50 milligrams

00:34:08.370 --> 00:34:15.900
of niacin amide, seven and one-half milligrams of riboflavin, and five  milligrams of thiamine.

00:34:15.900 --> 00:34:23.140
In a few instances, we have found it desirable
to inject 50 milligrams of ascorbic acid.

00:34:23.140 --> 00:34:30.040
Vitamin A deficiencies are usually of the
mild chronic type and therefore require months

00:34:30.050 --> 00:34:33.580
or even years for complete regression.

00:34:33.580 --> 00:34:41.160
Vitamin A should be administered in dosages
of 50,000 to 100,000 units daily.

00:34:41.160 --> 00:34:48.470
When a specific prompt return to health is
desired, vitamin therapy, either oral or parenteral,

00:34:48.470 --> 00:34:53.870
may reasonably be based on giving too much, too soon, and for too long,

00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:59.000
rather than too little, too late, and not long enough.

00:34:59.010 --> 00:35:04.170
We also administer a regular daily supplement of four to six ounces

00:35:04.170 --> 00:35:07.970
of dried brewer's yeast powder or oral liver extract.

00:35:08.380 --> 00:35:15.140
We mix the supplement with milk, tomato juice, or with food on the diet tray.

00:35:15.150 --> 00:35:18.710
A careful check is made on the amount of food returned.

00:35:18.740 --> 00:35:24.240
If the supplement has not been consumed, it is added at a later meal.

00:35:24.380 --> 00:35:34.260
In addition to the B vitamins, yeast and liver supply valuable amino acids, mineral salts, and enzymes.

00:35:34.270 --> 00:35:38.370
Crude liver extracts may be administered intramuscularly with good effect.

00:35:38.400 --> 00:35:43.480
Care should be taken to distinguish between preparations made

00:35:43.500 --> 00:35:47.840
by diluting potent USP antipernicious anemia liver extract

00:35:47.850 --> 00:35:52.950
and the comparatively unrefined liver extracts which contain more of the active B complex principles.

00:35:55.040 --> 00:36:00.250
The therapeutic value of these liver preparations
can be increased by the administration of

00:36:00.250 --> 00:36:05.220
thiamine, riboflavin, and niacin amide in
liberal dosage.

00:36:05.800 --> 00:36:13.520
In less severe deficiencies, we give a polyvitamin
formula supplying the daily adult allowances

00:36:13.520 --> 00:36:18.160
as recommended by the Food and Nutrition Board of the National Research Council.

00:36:18.360 --> 00:36:23.720
One, two, or three of these capsules are given daily.

00:36:23.720 --> 00:36:30.380
These recommended daily allowances should
not be confused with the minimum daily requirements

00:36:30.390 --> 00:36:37.770
set up for the package labeling purposes by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.

00:36:37.770 --> 00:36:42.730
Upon initial and subsequent examinations,
we endeavor to discover and correct,

00:36:42.840 --> 00:36:49.840
or give due consideration to conditioning factors which may contribute to the deficiency state.

00:36:49.850 --> 00:36:54.950
Finally, but perhaps most important of all,
we correct the patient's diet.

00:36:55.220 --> 00:37:02.300
Diet alone cannot ordinarily be depended upon to supply the needed vitamins in corrective dosage.

00:37:02.300 --> 00:37:06.880
But a liberal and well-balanced diet is an
essential element in this therapy.

00:37:07.160 --> 00:37:11.980
In a primary dietary deficiency, there can be no favorable prognosis

00:37:12.060 --> 00:37:17.420
unless the patient permanently improves his diet.

00:37:17.430 --> 00:37:23.260
This frequently presents a major management
problem when the patient rebels against changes

00:37:23.260 --> 00:37:24.720
in his dietary habits.

00:37:25.060 --> 00:37:30.580
[Dr. W.H. Sebrell:] What you say about the importance of diet is particularly interesting to me, Dr. Spies.

00:37:30.580 --> 00:37:35.660
You will recall a demonstration made by Ebbs, Tisdall, and Scott among

00:37:35.660 --> 00:37:41.640
210 women attending the ante-partum clinic at Toronto General Hospital.

00:37:41.650 --> 00:37:47.410
Analysis by the hospital staff had shown that
these women had been consuming a poor diet

00:37:47.410 --> 00:37:56.010
containing approximately 1600 to 1900 calories, 60 grams of protein, 500 milligrams of calcium,

00:37:56.010 --> 00:37:57.910
and ten milligrams of iron.

00:37:57.910 --> 00:38:06.040
These 210 women were divided into two groups.
In one group, no change was made in the diet.

00:38:06.040 --> 00:38:13.960
Those in the second group were furnished each day as a supplement, one egg, 30 ounces of milk,

00:38:13.960 --> 00:38:17.740
a half ounce of wheat germ, one ounce
of cheese,

00:38:17.780 --> 00:38:22.280
four-and-a-half ounces of canned tomatoes, and one orange.

00:38:22.280 --> 00:38:30.210
This dietary improvement increased their calories
from 1900 to 2600, the protein from 60 grams

00:38:30.210 --> 00:38:38.520
to 100 grams, calcium from 500 milligrams
to 1600 milligrams, and iron from 10 milligrams

00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:45.110
to 24 milligrams a day, besides materially
raising their vitamin intake.

00:38:45.110 --> 00:38:50.010
The table shows the effects of the poor diet
and of the supplemented diet.

00:38:50.010 --> 00:38:57.510
The 90 women whose diet had been supplemented had 30 percent less major complications during labor.

00:38:57.580 --> 00:39:04.760
no miscarriages or stillbirths, better
convalescence, fewer postpartum complications,

00:39:04.760 --> 00:39:09.310
and lost none of their babies during the
first six months.

00:39:09.310 --> 00:39:13.230
Such studies indicate the prevalence of suboptimal nutrition

00:39:13.230 --> 00:39:16.870
in a population group whose health is of special importance.

00:39:17.860 --> 00:39:23.220
They are significant as a modern demonstration of what may be achieved by better nutrition.

00:39:24.240 --> 00:39:27.480
[Dr. Robert Goodhart:] Evidence of this character is rapidly accumulating.

00:39:27.480 --> 00:39:31.500
Studies on nutrition and industry, dietary surveys, hospital records,

00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:35.400
all confirm the prevalence of nutritional deficiency.

00:39:35.440 --> 00:39:38.180
This evidence is now available to all in the
literature.

00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:42.640
It has been well-summarized by the Food Nutrition Board of the National Research Council.

00:39:43.740 --> 00:39:46.500
[Dr. Norman Jolliffe:] Such evidence is of
course necessary and proper.

00:39:46.600 --> 00:39:50.620
But any practicing physician who takes the trouble to familiarize himself

00:39:50.620 --> 00:39:56.660
with the objective lesions of vitamin deficiency can be convinced by his own observation.

00:39:56.670 --> 00:40:02.900
What troubles me most is the fact that some
physicians honestly inquire as to the significance

00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:04.910
of such widespread deficiency.

00:40:04.910 --> 00:40:10.180
[Dr. W.H. Sebrell:] Perhaps they overlook
the fact that disturbances in the body chemistry

00:40:10.180 --> 00:40:14.960
are well-advanced before even microscopic
tissue changes appear.

00:40:14.960 --> 00:40:18.660
[Dr. Robert Goodhart:] And perhaps we have all been too prone in the practice of medicine

00:40:18.660 --> 00:40:25.500
to let well enough alone. I remember our records
at Bellevue showing 17-1/2 cases of malnutrition

00:40:25.500 --> 00:40:30.340
per thousand discharges, which we all know represented only the most striking cases.

00:40:30.340 --> 00:40:35.830
[Dr. Normal Jolliffe:] Precisely. As Dr. Cruz
has pointed out and as we believe from own work,

00:40:35.830 --> 00:40:42.050
the mild and chronic forms of malnutrition
are accompanied by symptoms which are real handicaps.

00:40:42.280 --> 00:40:49.900
Photophobia, fatigability, emotional disturbances, the often-described neurasthenic syndrome

00:40:49.900 --> 00:40:53.520
and all its depressing personal and social
implications.

00:40:53.820 --> 00:40:57.740
[Dr. W.H. Sebrell:] Dr. Spies can tell us
something about the social importance of the

00:40:57.750 --> 00:41:00.680
nutritional problem, out of his experience
at Hillman.

00:41:00.680 --> 00:41:06.120
[Dr. Tom D. Spies:] I would say that Dr. Jolliffe has stated the case conservatively. As you

00:41:06.480 --> 00:41:12.320
As you know, we in Birmingham work in a comparatively restricted area.

00:41:12.320 --> 00:41:18.380
For seven years now, we've been able to observe
not only the results of therapy in the clinic

00:41:18.380 --> 00:41:23.150
but social and economic effects in the community
as well.

00:41:23.150 --> 00:41:29.770
We have to combat deeply implanted prejudice as well as severe economic limitations.

00:41:30.440 --> 00:41:35.960
For that reason, we physicians have employed
social workers and trained dietitians who

00:41:35.970 --> 00:41:41.690
who have maintained continuous personal contact with our patients and their families.

00:41:41.690 --> 00:41:46.150
Our problem is not solved. Perhaps, it may
never be.

00:41:46.400 --> 00:41:49.980
But the progress we have seen is unmistakable.

00:41:50.180 --> 00:41:58.060
Our pellagra death rate in severe uncomplicated cases, formerly 54 percent, is approaching zero.

00:41:58.300 --> 00:42:02.400
Many men who were unable to work have jobs in heavy industry,

00:42:02.520 --> 00:42:06.780
or have joined the armed forces or are paying income taxes.

00:42:07.080 --> 00:42:10.720
Mothers who did not care for their families now do so.

00:42:10.900 --> 00:42:15.340
Some children who failed to keep up with their classes are now making normal progress.

00:42:15.480 --> 00:42:19.320
One  of these boys is now a hotel manager, another is an engineer,

00:42:19.600 --> 00:42:22.560
and still another is a successful practicing physician.

00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:28.000
[Dr. Norman Jolliffe:] Could it be said, Dr.
Spies, that what you have observed is

00:42:28.010 --> 00:42:30.590
peculiar to a region in which pellagra is endemic?

00:42:30.900 --> 00:42:35.320
[Dr. Tom D. Spies:] I'm not speaking of pellagrins only. We do not know the incidence of pellagra

00:42:35.320 --> 00:42:40.280
in our community, and it is doubtful if it
is known in any mass population group.

00:42:40.480 --> 00:42:46.700
These people around Birmingham are not different from others. They are not constitutionally inferior.

00:42:46.700 --> 00:42:49.700
Their heredity is much the same
as yours and mine.

00:42:49.860 --> 00:42:53.240
Their problem is primarily one of malnutrition.

00:42:53.250 --> 00:42:57.050
With social and economic consequences which set up a vicious circle.

00:42:57.220 --> 00:43:00.420
Our job is to break that circle.

00:43:00.920 --> 00:43:04.120
[Dr. W.H. Sebrell:] Your opinion is supported
by experimental evidence.

00:43:04.360 --> 00:43:09.680
There was a test reported by Williams, Mason, Wyler and Smith from the Mayo Clini,

00:43:09.780 --> 00:43:15.000
where a group of women were kept on a special hospital diet for several months.

00:43:15.010 --> 00:43:19.730
The meals were certainly appetizing and only close scientific scrutiny

00:43:19.740 --> 00:43:23.120
would detect any serious nutritional defect.

00:43:23.120 --> 00:43:30.140
Nevertheless, on this diet, these women developed marked thiamine deficiency with all the classical symptoms

00:43:30.140 --> 00:43:35.700
ranging progressively from neurasthenic
manifestations to polyneuritis and psychotic conditions.

00:43:36.800 --> 00:43:41.760
At this point, they were unable to care for
themselves or perform any useful function

00:43:41.760 --> 00:43:46.910
in the community. When thiamine was administered,
the symptoms promptly regressed.

00:43:47.900 --> 00:43:52.840
[Dr. Robert Goodhart:] Other experiments now being conducted among large groups of industrial workers

00:43:52.840 --> 00:43:55.640
also support Dr. Spies' observation.

00:43:55.820 --> 00:43:59.260
In the field of industrial efficiency,

00:43:59.270 --> 00:44:04.090
the educational work of the national nutrition program for industry is one method of attack.

00:44:04.090 --> 00:44:09.970
We are attempting to assure adequate feeding for every employee in the industry,

00:44:10.220 --> 00:44:13.720
a task in which we need the local support of every physician.

00:44:14.700 --> 00:44:20.200
[Dr. W.H. Sebrell:] The federal government
is deeply concerned with this problem of better nutrition.

00:44:20.540 --> 00:44:23.660
We appeal to the medical profession for cooperation.

00:44:24.480 --> 00:44:29.940
A very definite step forward will have been
made when the physician becomes accustomed

00:44:29.950 --> 00:44:36.080
to looking for growth and microscopic evidences
of malnutrition in the eyes, in the mouth,

00:44:36.080 --> 00:44:41.329
on the skin, as well as for characteristic
nerve responses...

00:44:41.329 --> 00:44:46.030
and when the physician gives more than
a cursory glance at the patient's history

00:44:46.030 --> 00:44:52.320
as it relates to possible causes of nutritional deficiency, and when the physician prescribes

00:44:52.320 --> 00:44:55.830
diets adequate for the prevention of such
deficiencies.

00:44:57.020 --> 00:45:00.780
[Dr. Robert Goodhart:] And when the physician
recognizes the significance of all this for

00:45:00.790 --> 00:45:05.150
men and women engaged remotely or directly
in war work.

00:45:05.150 --> 00:45:11.040
[Dr. W.H. Sebrell:] Exactly. We are beginning
to learn that many persons without clinical

00:45:11.040 --> 00:45:16.470
evidence of disease are incompetent for the nation's need and inadequate to meet their

00:45:16.470 --> 00:45:21.540
own problems because of various forms of malnutrition.

00:45:21.540 --> 00:45:26.380
Chronic malnourishment has been found by careful medical observers among people

00:45:26.380 --> 00:45:30.040
in every walk of life, both children and adults.

00:45:30.040 --> 00:45:37.500
Through the knowledge now at hand, we can
eliminate much of the half-health, half-strength,

00:45:37.500 --> 00:45:43.130
and half-happiness which often results from
nutrition which is not quite good enough.

00:45:43.130 --> 00:45:55.890
[ Music ]

